      <h3>Tenant Fees</h3>
      <p>
        In accordance with the Tenant Fees Act 2019, the only fees a tenant may be charged are:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Holding Deposit:</strong> Up to one week's rent to reserve a property. This will be deducted from
          the first month's rent upon successful completion of the tenancy. The holding deposit will be retained if the
          tenant provides false or misleading information, fails a Right to Rent check, withdraws from the tenancy, or
          fails to take reasonable steps to enter into the tenancy agreement within 15 calendar days (or any agreed
          deadline).</li>
        <li><strong>Security Deposit:</strong> Equivalent to five weeks' rent (where annual rent is under £50,000) or
          six weeks' rent (where annual rent is £50,000 or above).</li>
        <li><strong>Rent:</strong> As agreed.</li>
        <li><strong>Changes to the tenancy (if requested by the tenant):</strong> £50 inc. VAT.</li>
        <li><strong>Early termination of the tenancy (if requested by the tenant):</strong> The landlord's reasonable
          costs of re-letting the property.</li>
        <li><strong>Utilities, council tax, communication services and TV licence:</strong> As applicable.</li>
        <li><strong>Default fees:</strong> Interest at 3% above the Bank of England base rate on outstanding rent after
          14 days, and the cost of replacing a lost key or security device.</li>
      </ul>

